      "uri": "https://sweet.io"
     },
     "description": "On December 30, 1981, Wayne Gretzky delivered a performance for the ages, etching his name even deeper into hockey history. Facing the Philadelphia Flyers at Northlands Coliseum, Gretzky erupted for an incredible five-goal night, reaching the unprecedented milestone of 50 goals in just 39 games. Each goal told a story: his first two came in the opening period to set the tone, his third helped Edmonton reclaim a two-goal advantage in the second, his fourth\u2014the game-winning goal\u2014highlighted his clutch play, and his fifth, an empty-netter with seconds remaining, sent the Edmonton Oilers faithful into a frenzy as \"The Great One\" shattered the NHL\u2019s previous record of 50 goals in 50 games.  \r\nAt just 20 years old, Gretzky\u2019s achievement showcased his unparalleled scoring ability, vision, and dominance over the game. That season, he would go on to set a staggering 92-goal record, solidifying his place as one of hockey's most extraordinary talents. Gretzky\u2019s 50-in-39 remains a defining moment in the sport\u2019s history\u2014a feat that redefined the limits of greatness and further established his legacy as a generational icon.\n\nOfficially Licensed Product of the NHL, NHLPA, and/or NHLAA. All copyright, logos, and marks are the property of their respective owners and are used, under license, by Sweet. All Rights Reserved. [Terms Apply](https://nhlbreakaway.com/terms).",
